cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "TOMShapeFlow-DEM: particle shape and angle of repose, a DEM study for lunar regolith handling"
abstract: >-
  Discrete-element (Chrono DEM-Engine) study of how grain shape sets the angle of repose of a granular
  material relevant to lunar regolith handling. Twelve multi-sphere grain shapes (Wadell roundness
  0.13 to 1.0 by aspect ratio 0.6 to 1.0, 2 mm grains) are tested in a rough-floor slump test,
  calibrated by rolling resistance to a 40 deg angle of repose (lunar highland simulant LHS-1: 39.6
  deg), with a lunar-gravity subset. Includes the simulation code, the clump templates, per-run
  results, a fitted design surface (angle = 46.0 - 4.3 R - 10.7 A, leave-one-out RMSE 1.6 deg) and the
  methods log. Code under MIT; shape templates and results under CC BY 4.0.
authors:
